  "code": "INELIG",
  "loc": "Abstract, p.667; Section 2 Preliminaries, p.669",
  "quote": "takes as input the metric \ud835\udc51 and outputs a distribution over all panels",
  "note": "The main object is a sortition (random panel selection) algorithm. Its input is a representation metric built from demographic features, not inputs submitted by agents and aggregated by voting. The paper notes a link to committee elections ('can be framed as a committee election problem'), but no voting procedure or voter inputs are modelled. Coding stopped."
